<title>PERU: Peru's November silver output falls 0.12 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's November silver output falls 0.12 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's silver output fell 0.12 percent to 169,150 tonnes in November compared to the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from Energy and Mines Ministry released Friday.</p>
<p>Production rose 2.62 percent to 1.785 million tonnes in the first 11 months of the year against the same period last year.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number two silver producer after Mexico. State-owned mining company Centromin Peru is the country's largest producer.</p>
<p>((Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134)) REUTER SH</p>
